// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/referral_program.t27 -- the referral graph, and what a referral may pay
; This contract owns the directed edge from one person to another: what the code that creates
; that edge may encode, how many times the ledger can record the same edge, which direction the
; status of an edge may move, whether a milestone can be taken back, and which currency a
; referral settles in. It owns NO amount -- not a per-referral payout, not a milestone bonus, not
; a welcome credit -- and the reason is recorded rather than assumed. It owns no /start grammar,
; no link, no ledger structure and no proof of identity; each of those has an owner named below
; and is consumed as a boolean. It writes down no account id, no handle and no referral code.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). Three structures in this domain assert something the code cannot do,
; and each was found by counting rather than by reading.
; 1. THE STATUS LADDER HAS A RUNG NOTHING CAN REACH. migrations/007_referral_events.sql:10 names
;    three statuses in the column's own comment, pending / confirmed / paid. FIVE read sites
;    branch on paid -- src/db/referrals.rs:423, :470, :484, :498 and :651, which is every counter
;    and every leaderboard the module has -- and ZERO writers produce it. The writers are
;    src/db/referrals.rs:268 (pending) and :345 (confirmed), plus the one-time backfill at
;    migrations/007_referral_events.sql:26 (confirmed). A sweep of src/ and migrations/ for a
;    statement that SETS this column to paid returns nothing at all. Until 2026-09-26
;    src/db/orders.rs:418 (at e39221e) documented the missing writer as though it ran: it stated
;    that confirm_referral set referral_events.status to paid, and the line it described -- today
;    src/db/referrals.rs:345, in confirm_referral_edge_in -- sets confirmed. That comment left with
;    R3's rewrite of the completion step. So half the module's WHERE clauses are dead branches,
;    and until R3 the completion path taught a lifecycle the database has never held.
; 2. THE EXPERIMENT RECORDS NOTHING IT CAN LATER READ. src/trios/referrals.rs:9-17 assigns a share
;    source deterministically per person so that A/B arms stay stable across sessions. It has
;    exactly ONE production caller, src/api/referrals.rs:71, which hands the arm to the client and
;    counts it on a metric. The referral_events table has a source column
;    (migrations/007_referral_events.sql:11) and exactly ONE production writer,
;    src/bot/commands.rs:201, which passes a fixed literal. The assigned arm is therefore never
;    stored against the event it was invented to label, and the funnel counter at
;    src/metrics.rs:140-144 carries a stage label and no arm. Every production row can hold one
;    single value of source, so no arm can ever be compared with another on any outcome.
; 3. THE ONE UNGATED ROUTE IS THE ONE THAT PUBLISHES THE ID. Four of the five registrations in
;    src/api/referrals.rs:22-43 call check_owner on the request headers (:68, :88, :124, :164)
;    before touching the graph. The leaderboard handler at src/api/referrals.rs:213-216 (at
;    8000ae8) takes State and Query, takes no HeaderMap, and calls no gate; no middleware supplies
;    one, because
;    api_routes at src/api/mod.rs:81-106 applies exactly one layer, a body limit at :105, the nest
;    that gives it its /api prefix carries none (src/api/mod.rs:77), and the layers in
;    src/main.rs:1157-1205 are alerting, request id, CORS, a response-header override, metrics and
;    header policy.
;    That route serializes TopReferrer whole (src/api/referrals.rs:238, :228 at 8000ae8), and
;    TopReferrer's first field is telegram_id (src/db/referrals.rs:22-28). One function away the
;    same module withholds that same field deliberately: src/db/referrals.rs:529-531 records that
;    the numeric id stays out of the invitee response, and the invitee route is owner-gated. The
;    field the gated route protects is published by the ungated one.
;    CLOSED 2026-09-26 by the owner's answer ("The referral top list", below): since then the
;    handler's first statement is check_admin, as the loyalty leaderboard's has been since R1, so a
;    caller without admin proof never reaches the serialization. The sentences of this item
;    describe the handler as it stood at 8000ae8, and the item's title is the 2026-09-21 reading.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Four readings, each re-measured against the line it names.
; 1. "the migrations that create them (survey points at 029, 035, 046)". 029 is wrong and two are
;    missing. migrations/029_order_idempotency_keys.sql is the checkout idempotency table -- its
;    header at :1 names POST /api/orders -- and a case-insensitive grep of that file for referral
;    returns 0. The two tables of this domain are created by migrations/007_referral_events.sql:4
;    and migrations/068_referral_milestones.sql:4. 035 and 046 are correctly named and neither
;    creates anything: 035 widens one column (:5-6), 046 rewrites values in place (:18-36).
; 2. "src/trios/referrals.rs (the deterministic share-source assignment, header around :3-6)".
;    The file's module doc is :1 and the function's doc comment is :3-8; :3-6 stops inside the
;    second paragraph. Small, but the sentence that matters for this contract -- that the return
;    is a clone so no caller holds a reference into config -- is at :7-8, outside the cited span.
; 3. "no milestone amount or threshold unless the repository publishes one -- measure
;    data/fleet_seed.json for 'referral' first". The measurement is real and I re-ran it:
;    data/fleet_seed.json (19434 bytes, the only file in data/) holds 0 occurrences of referral,
;    case-insensitive. (CORRECTED 2026-09-24: 19434 is a CRLF working copy's size; the committed
;    blob is 19084 bytes with 350 lines, as turbobaby/order-money's FLEET_SEED_BYTES now records.
;    The zero does not depend on line endings and still holds on the blob. The note constant below
;    keeps the reading as it was taken.) (READ AT e39221e: the ladder, its defaults and its award
;    were deleted on 2026-09-26, R3, and every src/db/referrals.rs line number in items 3 and 4
;    names that commit, not the tree.) The inference from that zero does not reach the ladder. The
;    THRESHOLDS were published, in exactly one place and on purpose: src/db/referrals.rs:712, whose own comment at
;    :705-711 records that there used to be three copies of this list and that the point of
;    collapsing them was to stop a fourth rung being promised by one copy and paid by none. That
;    list is declared below with its citation. The AMOUNTS are refused, and not because of the
;    seed zero -- they are refused because there is no single amount to declare: three different
;    numbers answer "what does rung N pay", the compiled default at src/db/referrals.rs:716, the
;    live shop value read from loyalty_config at :918-927, and the number actually credited, which
;    is frozen into the row at :810 and read back (get_referral_milestones, still live at :636).
;    src/api/referrals.rs:111-117 states the
;    same split in prose. A contract that named one of the three would be wrong about the other
;    two, which is the mistake the removed client-side table made.
; 4. The brief reads the ladder collapse as complete. It is not, by one list.
;    src/db/referrals.rs:716 is keyed by rung and so carries its own hand-written copy of the rung
;    numbers. A fourth rung added at :712 gets no default from :716. The config read does iterate
;    the ladder rather than the defaults (:918-927 loops MILESTONE_THRESHOLDS), so a live
;    loyalty_config key WOULD rescue the new rung -- which is why the predicate below requires both
;    sources to be absent rather than one. With neither, the map is seeded from :716 alone
;    (:900-901) and the rung resolves to zero at :799, maybe_award_referral_milestones skips a
;    non-positive amount at :800-802, and src/api/referrals.rs:145-151 (at e39221e) still published
;    the rung to the customer with that zero beside it. The promised-but-unpayable rung was still
;    reachable, through the defaults rather than through the ladder -- until R3 deleted both, and
;    since 2026-09-26 the route serves no rung at all (src/api/referrals.rs:144-151).
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It declares no per-referral bonus, no milestone bonus, no welcome
; credit and no currency conversion. It restates no part of the /start payload grammar: the
; prefix, the length bound on an incoming code and the conjunction that admits a referral belong
; to turbobaby/bot-surface, which owns start_records_a_referral, and arrive here as one boolean.
; It restates no link grammar, no payload character class and no landing: turbobaby/deeplink owns
; those and owns the link-side statement that a referral travels as an opaque code. It restates
; no ledger structure and no replay-key rule: turbobaby/loyalty-ledger owns the bonus ledger this
; domain wrote into until 2026-09-26. It restates no notice: turbobaby/notification-queue owns the
; friend-joined row this domain enqueues (and, until 2026-09-26, the friend-ordered and milestone
; rows), and this file states only where those enqueues sat relative to a money commit. It copies no window ceiling: turbobaby/star-award owns the only
; capped credit path in the corpus -- re-measured 2026-09-21 across all 43 .t27 files and still the
; only one, and re-run 2026-09-22 over the 45 and still the only one, so the absence claimed here
; is dated and not remembered -- and is named as precedent,
; with neither the size of its ceiling nor the
; size of its capped set reproduced here. It restates no identity proof: turbobaby/request-identity
; owns the gates, and this file records only which of its own routes stands behind one. It carries
; no leaderboard row, no rank, no
; person-level field, and no referral code fixture of any length -- a plausible eight-character
; string in a public spec is a code, and the alphabet is declared instead. Shipped Cyrillic
; strings in the cited sources are referred to by path and never quoted. No D14 material appears.
; --
; R3, THE OWNER'S ANSWER OF 2026-09-26 (DECISIONS.md, "R1-R3, the owner's answers of 2026-09-26").
; In translation (the Russian is verbatim in DECISIONS.md and in src/trios/referral_credit.rs): "it
; must be credited only for someone who rented, a 10% discount"; "the inviter can take it as a
; discount on a rental or as money"; and of the referral bonus points, "remove them, only the 10%
; discount". So since 2026-09-26 this domain writes no referral credit at all: confirming an edge
; pays nobody (confirm_referral_edge_in in src/db/referrals.rs replaced confirm_referral), the
; milestone ladder and its award are deleted, and the welcome credit is gone. The money a referral
; earns is turbobaby/referral-credit's: a THB ledger of its own, credited when a manager records a
; completed rental of an invited friend, at a rate that file owns. This file still owns the edge,
; its code, its status and its confirmation. The sections below on the three credits and the ladder
; are kept as the record of what shipped until then, and a src/db/referrals.rs or src/db/orders.rs
; line number in them that names deleted code is a reading of e39221e and says so.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-referral-program;

