; --- Reuse edges, named because there are no imports ---------------------------------------------
; A cross-contract dependency is a string pinned to its literal by a test. Each edge names the
; DECLARATION this file consumes, never a line in the sibling.
;
; RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21, from git rather than from memory, because the sentence that used to stand
; here ("ten contracts were written in parallel one wave ago and every line citation between them
; was stale within the hour") mixed one true count with one nobody timed. The true count: the wave
; before this one landed exactly TEN new contracts in a single commit. What that sentence left out
; is that this file's OWN wave landed THIRTEEN more beside it, so the hazard is larger than it
; said, not smaller -- a line number typed into a sibling was typed against a file another author
; was still editing. "Within the hour" is dropped: nobody measured the interval and this corpus does
; not publish guessed numbers.
;
; The corpus-wide RESIDUE is deliberately not pinned either, and the reason is the finding itself.
; It was counted at 63 when this correction began and at 7 a few minutes later, because sibling
; contracts are being repaired in parallel right now. A total written into this file would be false
; before the commit carrying it landed -- the same defect in a new costume. What is pinned is what
; cannot move: the wave sizes, which are git history, and this file's own contribution, which is
; zero. Citations into src/, migrations/, data/, docs/ and DECISIONS.md are a different case --
; those files were not moving -- and they stay.
pub const CORPUS_T27_FILE_COUNT : u8 = 43;
; Re-measured 2026-09-22 and deliberately NOT bound: a census of the corpus moves with every new
; contract. specs/ holds 45 .t27 files, all tracked. The two beyond the 43, order_presentation.t27
; and person_naming.t27, landed together in 14b01ac later on 2026-09-21 and belong to neither wave
; counted here (d1877db added ten, ed0ba9c thirteen). The star-award uniqueness sentence in the
; header was taken over the 43 and was re-run over the two new files the same day: neither declares
; a capped credit path (a case-insensitive grep for ceiling, capped or per-window returns 0 in
; both), so it still holds over the 45. The 43 is kept as the 2026-09-21 reading.
pub const CORPUS_T27_FILE_COUNT_REMEASURED : u8 = 45;
pub const CORPUS_T27_FILE_COUNT_REMEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
pub const STAR_AWARD_UNIQUENESS_RERUN_AT : str = "2026-09-22";
pub const PRIOR_WAVE_NEW_CONTRACTS : u8 = 10;
pub const OWN_WAVE_NEW_CONTRACTS : u8 = 13;
pub const SIBLING_LINE_CITATIONS_IN_THIS_FILE : u8 = 0;
pub const CORPUS_RESIDUE_IS_PINNED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const CORPUS_RESIDUE_NOTE : str = "Counted twice on 2026-09-21 during this correction: 63 at the start and 7 a few minutes later. The drop is sibling contracts being repaired in parallel, not a measurement error. A live corpus-wide total is therefore refused a constant here, because pinning one would publish a number that goes stale before the commit carrying it lands. Any reader who needs today's figure can grep for it in one line; what this file owes is the two numbers a grep cannot recover, and those are above.";
pub const WAVE_CENSUS_MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-21";
