; here -- "this file is not in that snapshot", written when the snapshot was taken before this file
; existed -- was true when written and false by the time it was read. That owner re-measured the
; same day: CONSUMER_COUNT went from 8 to 22, the array now names turbobaby/referral-program
; outright, and he keeps the superseded figure in CONSUMER_COUNT_BEFORE_THE_RE_MEASUREMENT so the
; move is visible rather than silent. A standing "is not in it" is exactly the false absence this
; corpus cannot afford, so the claim below carries the day it was taken and nothing here asserts an
; absence that only a date could make true.
